  "Question": "Monthly output increases from 100 to 144 over two months. What is the average monthly growth rate? (Set up and solve the equation \\(100(1+x)^2=144\\). Give the numerical value of the percentage; for example, write 15% as 15.)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "20",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "If \\(x\\) is the monthly growth rate as a decimal, each month multiplies output by \\(1+x\\). \\(100(1+x)^2=144\\), \\((1+x)^2=1.44\\), \\(1+x=\\pm1.2\\), so \\(x=0.2\\) or \\(x=-2.2\\) (discarded because it would give first-month output \\(100(1-2.2)=-120\\), but output cannot be negative). Therefore, the average monthly growth rate is 20%.",
